IMPORT prelude

-- Terrorism (Suppression of Bombings) Act 2007 (Singapore) -- what counts as an "explosive or other lethal device" and a protected
-- target (s 2), the terrorist bombing offence, its exclusions and its two fixed punishments (s 3), the duty of everyone in Singapore
-- to tell the police what they know and the protection for doing so (s 4), which offences are "terrorist bombing offences" and so
-- reach acts abroad (ss 2, 7), the political-offence and extradition deeming for Convention countries (ss 5, 6), and the Public
-- Prosecutor's consent (s 8).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1/7/2022), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/TSBA2007.txt. The deposit's legislative history lists the latest amendment as Act 17 of 2022
-- (Extradition (Amendment) Act 2022), in force 1 July 2022, which recast s 6(3), (6) and (8).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0121 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The Act is eight sections long, so nearly all of it is encoded. Not encoded: the mechanics of mutual
-- legal assistance under Part 3 of the Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act 2000 and of extradition under the Extradition Act
-- 1968 (only the deeming in ss 5 and 6 is encoded), s 6(4) and (6) (how a notification interacts with other notifications), and
-- what "material assistance", "major economic loss" or "extensive destruction" mean (taken as findings).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Terrorism (Suppression of Bombings) Act 2007 -- bombings`

§§ `2 -- explosive or other lethal device`

-- s 2: "explosive or other lethal device" means (a) "an explosive or other incendiary weapon or device that is designed, or has the
-- capability, to cause death, serious bodily injury, or substantial material damage"; or (b) a weapon or device so designed or
-- capable "through the release, dissemination, or impact of" (i) "toxic chemicals, biological agents or toxins or similar
-- substances"; or (ii) "radiation or radioactive material".
DECLARE Device HAS
    `is an explosive or incendiary weapon or device` IS A BOOLEAN
    `works by releasing toxic chemicals, biological agents or toxins` IS A BOOLEAN
    `works by releasing radiation or radioactive material` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is designed or capable to cause death, serious injury or substantial damage` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the device` IS A Device
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the device is an explosive or other lethal device` IF
        `the device`'s `is designed or capable to cause death, serious injury or substantial damage`
    AND (    `the device`'s `is an explosive or incendiary weapon or device`
         OR  `the device`'s `works by releasing toxic chemicals, biological agents or toxins`
         OR  `the device`'s `works by releasing radiation or radioactive material`)

§§ `2 -- the four protected kinds of target`

-- s 3(1)(a) to (d): "a place of public use", "a State or government facility", "a public transportation system", "an
-- infrastructure facility". s 2: a place of public use is any part of a building, land, street or waterway "accessible or open to
-- members of the public, whether continuously, periodically or occasionally, and whether for free or on payment of a charge",
-- including commercial, business, religious, entertainment and similar places "so accessible or open". A State or government
-- facility is "any conveyance or facility (whether permanent or temporary) used or occupied by" a government representative, Head
-- of State, minister, legislator, judge, or government or intergovernmental official "in connection with their official duties".
-- A public transportation system covers conveyances, facilities and objects "(whether publicly or privately owned)" used for
-- public transport of persons or cargo. An infrastructure facility is "any facility (whether publicly or privately owned)"
-- providing or distributing public services "such as water, sewage disposal, energy, fuel or communications".
DECLARE Target IS ONE OF
    `a shopping mall open to the public`
    `a concert hall open to ticket holders`
    `a visiting foreign minister's car on official business`
    `an MRT train`
    `a privately owned power station`
    `a private home`
    `a company's office closed to the public`

GIVEN `the target` IS A Target
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the target is protected by section 3` IF
    CONSIDER `the target`
    WHEN `a private home` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a company's office closed to the public` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3 -- terrorist bombing`

-- s 3(1): "Every person who intentionally and without lawful excuse delivers, places, discharges or detonates an explosive or other
-- lethal device in, into or against" a protected target "with intent to cause death or serious bodily injury, or extensive
-- destruction of such place, facility or system that results in or is likely to result in major economic loss" is guilty of an
-- offence.
-- s 3(2): (1) "does not apply to" (a) "the activities of armed forces during an armed conflict, as those terms are understood under
-- international humanitarian law, which are governed by that law"; or (b) "activities undertaken by military forces of a State in
-- the exercise of their official duties, to the extent that those activities are governed by other rules of international law".
-- s 2: "armed conflict" "does not include internal disturbances and tensions, such as riots, isolated and sporadic acts of
-- violence". "Military forces of a State" are (a) its armed forces; (b) "civilians who direct or organise" their official
-- activities; (c) civilians acting in support "if the civilians are under the formal command, control and responsibility of those
-- forces".
DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    `a private individual`
    `a member of a State's armed forces`
    `a civilian directing the armed forces' official activities`
    `a civilian supporting the armed forces under their formal command`
    `a civilian contractor supporting the armed forces outside their command`

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the actor is one of the military forces of a State` IF
    CONSIDER `the actor`
    WHEN `a private individual` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a civilian contractor supporting the armed forces outside their command` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE Bombing HAS
    `the actor` IS AN Actor
    `the device` IS A Device
    `the target` IS A Target
    `delivered, placed, discharged or detonated it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `did so intentionally` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended death or serious bodily injury` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended extensive destruction of the target` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the destruction results or is likely to result in major economic loss` IS A BOOLEAN
    `death was caused` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by armed forces in a conflict governed by international humanitarian law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the setting was only riots or internal disturbances` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the exercise of official duties governed by other international law` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the bombing` IS A Bombing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3(2) excludes the bombing` IF
        (    `the bombing`'s `by armed forces in a conflict governed by international humanitarian law`
         AND (NOT `the bombing`'s `the setting was only riots or internal disturbances`))
    OR  (    `the actor is one of the military forces of a State` (`the bombing`'s `the actor`)
         AND `the bombing`'s `in the exercise of official duties governed by other international law`)

GIVEN `the bombing` IS A Bombing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bombing has the required intent` IF
        `the bombing`'s `intended death or serious bodily injury`
    OR  (    `the bombing`'s `intended extensive destruction of the target`
         AND `the bombing`'s `the destruction results or is likely to result in major economic loss`)

GIVEN `the bombing` IS A Bombing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bombing is an offence under section 3` IF
        `the bombing`'s `delivered, placed, discharged or detonated it`
    AND `the bombing`'s `did so intentionally`
    AND (NOT `the bombing`'s `had a lawful excuse`)
    AND `the device is an explosive or other lethal device` (`the bombing`'s `the device`)
    AND `the target is protected by section 3` (`the bombing`'s `the target`)
    AND `the bombing has the required intent` `the bombing`
    AND (NOT `section 3(2) excludes the bombing` `the bombing`)

-- s 3(1): on conviction the offender "(e) if he or she had intended to cause death or serious bodily injury and death is caused, be
-- punished with death; or (f) in any other case, be punished with life imprisonment". Both are fixed: the text gives no lesser
-- alternative and no maximum.
DECLARE Punishment IS ONE OF
    `death`
    `life imprisonment`
    `none under section 3`

GIVEN `the bombing` IS A Bombing
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment under section 3` MEANS
    IF NOT `the bombing is an offence under section 3` `the bombing` THEN `none under section 3`
    ELSE IF `the bombing`'s `intended death or serious bodily injury` AND `the bombing`'s `death was caused` THEN `death`
         ELSE `life imprisonment`

§§ `2, 7 -- terrorist bombing offences, and acts abroad`

-- s 2: "terrorist bombing offence" means (a) an offence under s 3; (b) conspiracy, (c) inciting another, (d) attempting, or (e)
-- "aiding, abetting, counselling or procuring the commission of" one. The s 4 failure to disclose is not on the list.
-- s 7: "Every person who, outside Singapore, commits an act or omission that, if committed in Singapore, would constitute a
-- terrorist bombing offence is deemed to commit the act or omission in Singapore". There is no nationality condition.
-- s 4(1) applies only to a person "in Singapore".
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `committing a section 3 bombing`
    `conspiring to commit one`
    `inciting another to commit one`
    `attempting one`
    `aiding, abetting, counselling or procuring one`
    `failing to disclose information under section 4`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is a terrorist bombing offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `failing to disclose information under section 4` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `it happened in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct can be tried in Singapore` IF
        `it happened in Singapore`
    OR  `the conduct is a terrorist bombing offence` `the conduct`

§§ `4 -- the duty to disclose information`

-- s 4(1): "Every person in Singapore who has information which the person knows or believes may be of material assistance" (a) "in
-- preventing the commission by another person of a terrorist bombing offence"; or (b) "in securing the apprehension, prosecution or
-- conviction of another person, in Singapore, for a terrorist bombing offence", "and who fails to disclose the information
-- immediately to a police officer" commits an offence: "a fine not exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- 5 years or to both". The text gives no defence of reasonable excuse and no exception for legal privilege.
DECLARE Witness HAS
    `is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knows or believes the information may help prevent another's offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knows or believes the information may help bring another to justice in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `disclosed it immediately to a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the witness` IS A Witness
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the witness commits the section 4 offence` IF
        `the witness`'s `is in Singapore`
    AND (    `the witness`'s `knows or believes the information may help prevent another's offence`
         OR  `the witness`'s `knows or believes the information may help bring another to justice in Singapore`)
    AND (NOT `the witness`'s `disclosed it immediately to a police officer`)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum section 4 fine` MEANS 50000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum section 4 imprisonment in years` MEANS 5

GIVEN `fine imposed` IS A NUMBER, `years imposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 4 sentence is within the maximum` IF
        `fine imposed` AT MOST `the maximum section 4 fine`
    AND `years imposed` AT MOST `the maximum section 4 imprisonment in years`

-- s 4(2): "No criminal or civil proceedings shall lie against a person for any disclosure made in good faith under this section."
-- s 4(3): such a person "is not to be treated as being in breach of any restriction upon the disclosure of information imposed by
-- law, contract or rules of professional conduct".
GIVEN `made under section 4` IS A BOOLEAN, `made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the discloser is protected from proceedings and confidentiality breach` IF
    `made under section 4` AND `made in good faith`

§§ `5, 6 -- Convention countries: assistance and extradition`

-- s 5(1): for assistance to a foreign country under Part 3 of the Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act 2000, a "relevant
-- offence" of that country "is deemed not to be an offence of a political character". s 6(7)(b): for the Extradition Act 1968 a
-- relevant offence of a Convention country so applied "is deemed not to be an offence of a political character".
-- s 6(8): a "relevant offence" is a foreign offence where the act or omission, if in Singapore, would "(a) constitute a terrorist
-- bombing offence; or (b) be such an offence if the description concerned contained a reference to any intent or state of mind
-- ... or to any circumstance of aggravation, necessary to constitute the offence".
GIVEN `would be a terrorist bombing offence in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `would be one but for a missing intent or aggravation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the foreign offence is a relevant offence` IF
    `would be a terrorist bombing offence in Singapore` OR `would be one but for a missing intent or aggravation`

GIVEN `is a relevant offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the political-offence objection is available` IF
    NOT `is a relevant offence`

-- s 6(2): "where no extradition treaty is in force between Singapore and a Convention country", a Gazette notification under s 4
-- of the Extradition Act 1968 "may be made" applying that Act as if there were a treaty; s 6(5): likewise where a treaty is in force
-- but "does not provide for the extradition of persons accused of or convicted of a relevant offence".
GIVEN `is a Convention country` IS A BOOLEAN, `a treaty is in force` IS A BOOLEAN, `the treaty covers relevant offences` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Gazette notification may apply the Extradition Act` IF
        `is a Convention country`
    AND (    (NOT `a treaty is in force`)
         OR  (NOT `the treaty covers relevant offences`))

§§ `8 -- the Public Prosecutor's consent`

-- s 8: "A prosecution under this Act must not be instituted except by or with the consent of the Public Prosecutor."
GIVEN `instituted by the Public Prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN, `with the Public Prosecutor's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prosecution may be instituted` IF
    `instituted by the Public Prosecutor` OR `with the Public Prosecutor's consent`
